        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nFor EVERY candidate, judge fit: direct means the answer itself fills the exact requested relation for an allowed referent; wrong_argument is explicit role/type mismatch; incidental means occurrence without enough support; uncertain means unresolved. Select support only for an original segment positively assigning this candidate to the requested relation; otherwise empty. Select counter only for actual counterevidence, not mere absence. conflict=same_referent only for incompatible claims for the same entity/attribute/relevant scope, not legitimate namesakes or complementary facts. entity labels are provisional groups, not truth. scope=excluded only for an explicit question constraint, with constraint selecting a literal numeric phrase from the question; otherwise allowed/unknown. observed_slot describes the answer's ACTUAL role, not the role wanted by the question. Mere disagreement does not make a source false. Fill all opaque keys.\nIndependent polarity defense: for each candidate scan ALL documents for a positive assignment to the requested role. Positive assignment for an allowed distinct referent must be fit=direct and placed in SUPPORT even if the candidate is not famous or not in the first document. A support statement is not a counter. Counter requires an explicit negative/exclusion or incompatible statement about that exact referent, and cannot be justified by absence. A birth header (date1 - date2) supports date1, not merely prose Born on. Distinct people sharing a name, distinct works with one title, multiple sports and plural mascots may legitimately coexist. Role match and truth are separate axes: competing same-role values stay direct with conflict flagged. Unknown memory is not negative evidence. Recheck all wrong_argument labels against the source before returning.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who is the main character in the video game \\\"Who Framed Roger Rabbit\\\"?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 173, \"text\": \"Who Framed Roger Rabbit (1988 video game) Who Framed Roger Rabbit is a video game based on the film of the same name for MS-DOS, Amiga, Atari ST, Apple II, and Commodore 64.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d00\", \"start\": 174, \"end\": 222, \"text\": \"It was released by Buena Vista Software in 1988.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d00\", \"start\": 223, \"end\": 321, \"text\": \"The player controls Roger Rabbit through four levels, each with its own specific task to complete.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d00\", \"start\": 322, \"end\": 502, \"text\": \"In the first level, the player must drive Benny the Cab to reach the Ink and Paint Club ahead of the Toon Patrol, jumping and swerving to avoid cars and puddles of Dip in the road.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d00\", \"start\": 503, \"end\": 533, \"text\": \"The second level is set within\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 183, \"text\": \"Who Framed Roger Rabbit (1989 video game) Who Framed Roger Rabbit is an action-adventure video game created for the Nintendo Entertainment System by Rare and published by LJN in 1989.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d01\", \"start\": 184, \"end\": 368, \"text\": \"The single-player game is loosely based on the film of the same name and had combined elements of graphic adventure computer games with some more traditional action adventure gameplay.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d01\", \"start\": 369, \"end\": 456, \"text\": \"A different version of the game was also released for various computer systems in 1988.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d01\", \"start\": 457, \"end\": 501, \"text\": \"The game takes place in Los Angeles in 1947.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d01\", \"start\": 502, \"end\": 602, \"text\": \"The player controls private detective Eddie Valiant, who is always closely followed by Roger Rabbit.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d01\", \"start\": 603, \"end\": 611, \"text\": \"The game\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Roger Rabbit\", \"scope\": \"main character\", \"claim\": \"The player controls Roger Rabbit through four levels in the video game Who Framed Roger Rabbit.\", \"answer\": \"Roger Rabbit\", \"quote\": \"The player controls Roger Rabbit through four levels, each with its own specific task to complete.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0120-2dd949c465b0:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Eddie Valiant\", \"scope\": \"main character\", \"claim\": \"The player controls private detective Eddie Valiant in the video game Who Framed Roger Rabbit.\", \"answer\": \"Eddie Valiant\", \"quote\": \"The player controls private detective Eddie Valiant, who is always closely followed by Roger Rabbit.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Roger Rabbit\", \"Eddie Valiant\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Eddie Valiant\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Roger Rabbit\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
